 - `complete` when the Goal has at least one live DQ as a child and every live DQ whose parent is the Goal is `answered`; a Goal with no live top-level DQ is `in_progress`, because nothing has been asked yet. It reads no line: a line of the Goal is owed on each top-level question as a `limit` item (§8.1) and the select waits on it, and the owner's "met" is a complete Goal with no line under OWED. hyp stores no word for it. Sub-questions are covered through the `answered` rule of §7.4, so sub-questions under rejected rival hypotheses never block the Goal. (This clarifies the advice's "nothing stale" clause: stale on the selected path already prevents `answered`.)
 - Otherwise `in_progress`, with counts per DQ state over all DQs and a count of stale live nodes.
-- **Constraints block.** A Goal body's constraints block runs from the first line that starts with `May change:`, `Read only:` or `Never:` to the end of the body. It is valid when it holds each of the three headings and every non-empty line in it starts with one of them. Replay stores no word for it and no status reads it. `hyp add goal` admits any body and warns when the body has a heading but no valid block. `hyp prompt G --actor A` prints the `/goal` prompt for G from G's node and the store's place in its repository: the store's path relative to the repository root, A, G, the skill hyp-goal-run, the stop clauses, and each block line as written, in body order; `--branch` and `--pr` add a clause each after the block. It refuses with exit 1 and nothing on stdout when the block is missing or not valid, naming each problem, and exits 2 with no `--actor` (it does not read `$HYP_ACTOR`), for an id that is not a Goal, or for a `--branch` that holds a space or a control character. It exits 3 when no repository holds the store. Lines split on `\n`, and a line is empty only when it holds no byte, so a line of spaces, a tab, or the lone `\r` of a blank line in a CRLF body is a bad line inside the block. The store's path is read after resolving symbolic links, so a store reached through a linked directory prints the same bytes. It reads no answer, so the same Goal and flags print the same bytes before and after an answer and in a store with other Goals.
